@dataclass(repr=False)
class Tender(IdentifiedObject):
    '''
    Tender is what is "offered" by the customer towards making a payment and
    is often more than the required payment (hence the need for 'change').
    The payment is thus that part of the Tender that goes towards settlement
    of a particular transaction.
    Tender is modelled as an aggregation of Cheque and Card. Both these tender
    types can exist in a single tender bid thus 'accountHolderName' has to
    exist separately in each of Cheque and Card as each could have a different
    account holder name.
    '''

